On Wed, May 12, 2004 at 09:55:47PM +0200, Karol Kozimor wrote:
> question: the ICH3-M spec specifies the PM2_CNT address at PMBASE + 0x20,
> just before the GPE block. This seems consistent with my FADT, which places
> PMBASE at 0xe400 and GPE0_BLK at 0xe428. Would manual poking at the
> presumed location of ARB_DIS or FADT override work?

Maybe. On the other hand, your BIOS / hardware vendor likely disallowed C3
for a reason, e.g. some hardware which doesn't work flawlessly with ARB_DIS.
Note, for example, that the ipw2100 project ( http://ipw2100.sf.net )
suffers from some strange C3-related errors.

